{"data": [{"id": "2122134686948581874", "author_id": "1630408249940799489", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk @hexassistant there is a whole world of cool things for us to utilize. uisdk behaviors are particularly valuable primitives", "created_at": "2026-11-16T01:08:31.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/avgvstvs96/status/2122134686948581874", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122122985507106988", "author_id": "17824785", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Incredible", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:22:01.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/dwlz/status/2122122985507106988", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122113314624847885", "author_id": "1519357823087489027", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Any reason you used Argon over Carbon?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:43:35.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/Zapidroid/status/2122113314624847885", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122107932389384674", "author_id": "1239725529798004736", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk two prompts to undo twenty years of product management, this is great", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:22:12.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/tofuuuuh/status/2122107932389384674", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122098094372163646", "author_id": "1279688197795188737", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk This is amazing", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:43:07.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/akinayoUI/status/2122098094372163646", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122088056245117367", "author_id": "56134869", "text": "@lxe @rauchg @uisdk You should check https://t.co/DyGmYaQKaT then. It even has a Winamp Skin Museum.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:03:13.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/IvanMontilla/status/2122088056245117367", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122087329884221865", "author_id": "7232882", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Oh am I so absolutely ready for UI to go back to making me feel emotions again", "created_at": "2026-11-15T22:00:20.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/lxe/status/2122087329884221865", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 143, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122086228279558597", "author_id": "14040602", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Patterns for a pattern-recognition machine.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:55:57.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/pablopoo/status/2122086228279558597", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122074271816253560", "author_id": "91763440", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Two prompts to a working Winamp clone with 14 reusable behaviors is the part that gets me. The agent is not just generating UI, it is composing real components. This is what agentic UI was supposed to feel like from the start.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:08:27.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/bijaypandey/status/2122074271816253560", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122068897289642342", "author_id": "1991210188578467840", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Reusing 14 tested behaviors instead of hand-rolling them is the real win, since agents usually get focus and keyboard handling subtly wrong. Did the result hold up with keyboard-only and a screen reader, or does it just look right?", "created_at": "2026-11-15T20:47:05.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/viral_warden/status/2122068897289642342", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122051368513061273", "author_id": "2111273592948400128", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Getting 14 behaviors for free is the real win. Agent-built UIs usually fall apart on exactly those details: focus handling, typeahead, keyboard nav. Having them built in turns a demo into something usable.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:37:26.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/WhichAITools/status/2122051368513061273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122045787240878221", "author_id": "1689723696275976192", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk two prompts and 14 behaviors. still had to tell it which window to resize", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:15:16.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/__harsh020__/status/2122045787240878221", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 165, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122045435745599981", "author_id": "1728475650", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk An agent is only as good as the primitives it can find. Focus handling and ARIA are easy to get wrong from scratch, so reusing tested behaviours beats generating them. The harder part is catching an agent that breaks a11y on the second or third edit.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:13:52.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ivastintech/status/2122045435745599981", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122044923746652526", "author_id": "1728593911", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Shu &amp; Shadcn, the goats", "created_at": "2026-11-15T19:11:50.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/AAorris/status/2122044923746652526", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122037904839180604", "author_id": "892153111", "text": "@rauchg @uisdk Hey Guillermo, is it possible to use UI SDK without a JS framework?\n\nfor example say have some legacy php projects, I would like to use it on there.\n\nalternative do you support @tailwindcss ? I use it in quite a few projects for the front end in python apps.", "created_at": "2026-11-15T18:43:56.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ErikThiart/status/2122037904839180604", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 80, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1630408249940799489", "username": "avgvstvs96", "name": "bassim", "verified": false}, {"id": "15540222", "username": "rauchg", "name": "Guillermo Rauch", "verified": false}, {"id": "2120243570158538752", "username": "uisdk", "name": "UI SDK", "verified": false}, {"id": "2118483050405490688", "username": "hexassistant", "name": "hex", "verified": false}, {"id": "17824785", "username": "dwlz", "name": "Dan Loewenherz", "verified": false}, {"id": "1519357823087489027", "username": "Zapidroid", "name": "Zapidroid", "verified": false}, {"id": "1239725529798004736", "username": "tofuuuuh", "name": "Mike", "verified": false}, {"id": "1279688197795188737", "username": "akinayoUI", "name": "AkinAyo | UI/UX Designer", "verified": false}, {"id": "56134869", "username": "IvanMontilla", "name": "Ivan • AI", "verified": false}, {"id": "7232882", "username": "lxe", "name": "Aleksey Smolenchuk", "verified": false}, {"id": "14040602", "username": "pablopoo", "name": "Pablo Poo", "verified": false}, {"id": "91763440", "username": "bijaypandey", "name": "Bijay Pandey", "verified": false}, {"id": "1991210188578467840", "username": "viral_warden", "name": "Viral Warden", "verified": false}, {"id": "2111273592948400128", "username": "WhichAITools", "name": "Leilani", "verified": false}, {"id": "1689723696275976192", "username": "__harsh020__", "name": "harsh", "verified": false}, {"id": "1728475650", "username": "ivastintech", "name": "Ivastin Tech", "verified": false}, {"id": "1728593911", "username": "AAorris", "name": "Aaron Morris", "verified": false}, {"id": "892153111", "username": "ErikThiart", "name": "Erik Thiart", "verified": false}, {"id": "895273477711769600", "username": "tailwindcss", "name": "Tailwind CSS", "verified": true}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2122134686948581874", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzow6925nlckvuubp33hn0l03guwt", "oldest_id": "2122037904839180604", "result_count": 15}}